# Every live external_body in kernel/verified, checked by tools/check-external-body.py against the
# reason line beside each attribute. Fields, separated by tabs: path under kernel/verified, item,
# class, reason.
#
# glue      hardware or assembly leaf glue, the only unverified code CLAUDE.md allows
# gap       uses something this Verus cannot check: a raw pointer, a conjured permission, uninit memory
# unproven  plain code or a lemma with no proof yet, so proof debt
arch/x86_64.rs	flush_every_context	glue	only the hardware can attest a flush, so only this makes the token
arch/x86_64.rs	serial_write	glue	writes the serial port through port I/O, which has no state a proof could see
arch/x86_64.rs	zeroed	gap	builds a value from zeroed memory, which Verus cannot check
array.rs	new	gap	builds a value from zeroed memory, which Verus cannot check
capability/kernel.rs	invalidate_iommu_all	glue	only the IOMMU can attest an invalidate, so only this makes its token
pagetable/pagemap_util_t.rs	page_map_set	glue	writes a hardware page table through a raw pointer
pagetable/pagemap_util_t.rs	page_map_set_no_requires	glue	writes a hardware page table through a raw pointer
pagetable/pagemap_util_t.rs	page_map_take	glue	clears a hardware page table word and returns it in one atomic exchange, since another core's walk may set the accessed or dirty bit between a read and a write
pagetable/pagemap_util_t.rs	page_map_take_status	glue	clears the processor's accessed and dirty bits in a hardware page table word atomically, since another core's walk may set one between a read and a write
pagetable/pagemap_util_t.rs	page_perm_to_page_map	glue	writes a hardware page table through a raw pointer
queue_lock.rs	spin_hint	glue	the pause instruction, which has no state a proof could see
